{{!-- Three more posts on the same subject.

"Related" has to mean something a publication controls, and the only relation Ghost stores is
the tag. So this is the primary tag's three most recent other posts — not a random draw, not
"latest", both of which would put the same three cards under every post on the site.

Two details in the filter carry weight:

  - `id:-{{id}}` excludes the post being read. One `id:-` term is also the exact shape
	core/frontend/helpers/get.js optimises, so this stays a cacheable query.
  - `tags:[…]` on the PRIMARY tag, not on all of them. Filtering on the full tag list widens
	the match until "related" means "shares any word", and it is what makes the result depend
	on tag ORDER, which is invisible to the person who set it.

An untagged post has no relation to draw on and renders nothing — the same honest outcome as
an empty menu losing its footer column. --}}
{{#if primary_tag}}
	{{!-- Both paths are read from the post's own context. The {{#get}} helper resolves the
	mustaches in its filter through a resolver of its own, and that resolver understands a plain
	path and a dotted one and nothing else: written inside {{#primary_tag}}, where the tag's slug
	is `{{slug}}` and the post's id is one frame up, `{{../id}}` fails the render outright with
	`unsupported path segment ""` — a 200 with a hole in it. --}}
	{{#get "posts" filter="tags:[{{primary_tag.slug}}]+id:-{{id}}" limit="3" include="tags" as |related|}}
		{{#if related}}
			<section
				aria-labelledby="rel-head"
				class="container pt-20">
				<h2
					id="rel-head"
					class="font-ui text-muted mb-6 text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.16em] uppercase">{{t "Related reading"}}</h2>

				<div class="grid grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(280px,100%),1fr))] gap-6">
					{{#foreach related}}
						<article class="{{post_class}} border-border bg-surface overflow-hidden rounded-md border">
							<a
								href="{{url}}"
								class="text-text block no-underline">
								{{#if feature_image}}
									<img
										src="{{img_url feature_image size="l"}}"
										{{> "image-srcset" image=feature_image sizes="(min-width: 768px) 410px, 100vw"}}
										{{#if feature_image_alt}}alt="{{feature_image_alt}}"{{else}}alt=""{{/if}}
										loading="lazy"
										decoding="async"
										class="border-border block aspect-video w-full border-b object-cover">
								{{/if}}

								<div class="p-5">
									{{#primary_tag}}
										<span class="font-meta text-meta tracking-meta text-accent uppercase">{{name}}</span>
									{{/primary_tag}}

									<h3 class="font-display tracking-heading mt-2.5 text-xl leading-[1.26] font-medium">{{title}}</h3>

									<p class="font-meta text-meta tracking-meta text-muted mt-3 uppercase">
										{{date format="DD MMM YYYY"}}
										<span aria-hidden="true"> · </span>
										{{reading_time seconds=(t "< 1 min read") minute=(t "1 min read") minutes=(t "% min read")}}
									</p>
								</div>
							</a>
						</article>
					{{/foreach}}
				</div>
			</section>
		{{/if}}
	{{/get}}
{{/if}}
